  m_text: "<b>Season:</b> Summer (June\u2013September)\n<b>Path:</b> Asian landmass
    heats up, creating a powerful low-pressure system over it. The winds are drawn
    from the cooler, high-pressure ocean towards the hot land which condenses over
    the warmer land and falls in the form of heavy monsoon rains. \nSouthern Indian
    Ocean \u2192 Peninsular India \u2192 Northern India\n<b>Examples: </b>Kerala
    (first to receive), most of India receives monsoon\nwinds."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
